<h2>How to think about it</h2>

<p>A Kenyan producer's problem is rarely a shortage of tea. It is reaching the specific importer whose blend needs what that estate actually produces. A Chinese buyer's problem is the mirror image: finding a supplier who can meet a grade, a volume and a documentation standard at the same time. Matchmaking exists to shorten that search from months of correspondence to a scheduled half-hour.</p>

